cells = [
    {
        "cell_type": "markdown",
        "metadata": {},
        "source": [
            "# 🧠 TP53 Deep Learning Architecture & Predictive Modelling\n\n",
            "## Exploratory Deep-Learning Framework for Comparative TP53 Sequence Analysis\n\n",
            "**Research Project:** Elephant TP53 Hotspot Mapping  \n",
            "**Researcher:** Ritika Rajendra Rawat  \n",
            "**Degree:** MSc Bioinformatics  \n",
            "**Institution:** University of Mumbai\n\n",
            "---\n\n",
            "## 🎯 Research Objective\n\n",
            "This notebook develops an exploratory deep-learning and predictive-modelling framework for representing TP53-related protein sequences computationally.\n\n",
            "The workflow investigates how amino-acid sequences can be transformed into numerical representations and analysed using neural-network-based feature learning.\n\n",
            "The framework includes sequence encoding, embedding-based representation, convolutional feature extraction, latent representation, dimensionality reduction, architecture design, and reproducible result export.\n\n",
            "> ⚠️ The current sequence dataset is not sufficiently large or independently labelled to support claims of clinically validated predictive performance. The deep-learning component is therefore treated as a methodological prototype."
        ]
    },
    {
        "cell_type": "markdown",
        "metadata": {},
        "source": [
            "## 🧬 Scientific Rationale\n\n",
            "TP53 is a highly conserved tumour-suppressor protein with an important role in genome integrity, cell-cycle regulation, apoptosis, and cancer biology.\n\n",
            "Comparative sequence analysis provides an initial computational framework for investigating conservation and divergence across species.\n\n",
            "Deep-learning methods can potentially learn hierarchical representations directly from biological sequences. Meaningful predictive modelling, however, requires appropriately labelled datasets, sufficient sample size, careful experimental design, independent validation, and biologically interpretable endpoints.\n\n",
            "This notebook therefore separates representation learning from validated prediction."
        ]
    },
    {
        "cell_type": "code",
        "execution_count": None,
        "metadata": {},
        "outputs": [],
        "source": [
            "from pathlib import Path\n",
            "import warnings\n",
            "import random\n",
            "\n",
            "warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\n",
            "\n",
            "import numpy as np\n",
            "import pandas as pd\n",
            "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
            "\n",
            "from Bio import SeqIO\n",
            "from sklearn.decomposition import PCA\n",
            "\n",
            "import tensorflow as tf\n",
            "from tensorflow.keras import layers, models\n",
            "from tensorflow.keras.utils import pad_sequences\n",
            "\n",
            "print('TensorFlow:', tf.__version__)\n",
            "print('Libraries loaded successfully.')"
        ]
    },
    {
        "cell_type": "code",
        "execution_count": None,
        "metadata": {},
        "outputs": [],
        "source": [
            "SEED = 42\n",
            "random.seed(SEED)\n",
            "np.random.seed(SEED)\n",
            "tf.random.set_seed(SEED)\n",
            "\n",
            "print('Reproducibility seed:', SEED)"
        ]
    },
    {
        "cell_type": "code",
        "execution_count": None,
        "metadata": {},
        "outputs": [],
        "source": [
            "def find_repository_root():\n",
            "    current = Path.cwd().resolve()\n",
            "    candidates = [\n",
            "        current,\n",
            "        current.parent,\n",
            "        current.parent.parent,\n",
            "        current.parent.parent.parent,\n",
            "    ]\n",
            "    for path in candidates:\n",
            "        if (path / 'data').exists() and (path / 'README.md').exists():\n",
            "            return path\n",
            "    raise FileNotFoundError('Could not locate the repository root.')\n",
            "\n",
            "ROOT = find_repository_root()\n",
            "DATA_DIR = ROOT / 'data'\n",
            "PROCESSED_DIR = DATA_DIR / 'processed'\n",
            "RESULTS_DIR = ROOT / 'results'\n",
            "FIGURES_DIR = ROOT / 'figures'\n",
            "\n",
            "RESULTS_DIR.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n",
            "FIGURES_DIR.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n",
            "\n",
            "INPUT_FASTA = PROCESSED_DIR / 'TP53_clean.fasta'\n",
            "\n",
            "print('Repository:', ROOT)\n",
            "print('Input FASTA:', INPUT_FASTA)"
        ]
    },
    {
        "cell_type": "code",
        "execution_count": None,
        "metadata": {},
        "outputs": [],
        "source": [
            "if not INPUT_FASTA.exists():\n",
            "    raise FileNotFoundError(f'Input FASTA was not found: {INPUT_FASTA}')\n",
            "\n",
            "records = list(SeqIO.parse(INPUT_FASTA, 'fasta'))\n",
            "print('Number of sequences:', len(records))\n",
            "\n",
            "for record in records:\n",
            "    print(f'{record.id}: {len(record.seq)} amino acids')"
        ]
    },
    {
        "cell_type": "markdown",
        "metadata": {},
        "source": [
            "# 🔎 Sequence Quality Control\n\n",
            "Only standard amino-acid residues are retained for numerical encoding."
        ]
    },
    {
        "cell_type": "code",
        "execution_count": None,
        "metadata": {},
        "outputs": [],
        "source": [
            "AMINO_ACIDS = 'ACDEFGHIKLMNPQRSTVWY'\n",
            "VALID_AMINO_ACIDS = set(AMINO_ACIDS)\n",
            "\n",
            "def clean_sequence(sequence):\n",
            "    return str(sequence).upper().replace(' ', '').replace('\\n', '')\n",
            "\n",
            "cleaned_records = []\n",
            "\n",
            "for record in records:\n",
            "    sequence = clean_sequence(record.seq)\n",
            "    invalid = set(sequence) - VALID_AMINO_ACIDS\n",
            "    if invalid:\n",
            "        print(f'Excluded {record.id}: invalid residues = {sorted(invalid)}')\n",
            "        continue\n",
            "    cleaned_records.append({\n",
            "        'id': record.id,\n",
            "        'description': record.description,\n",
            "        'sequence': sequence,\n",
            "    })\n",
            "\n",
            "print('Valid sequences retained:', len(cleaned_records))"
        ]
    },
    {
        "cell_type": "markdown",
        "metadata": {},
        "source": [
            "# 🔢 Amino-Acid Encoding\n\n",
            "Each amino acid is mapped to an integer token. Zero is reserved for padding."
        ]
    },
    {
        "cell_type": "code",
        "execution_count": None,
        "metadata": {},
        "outputs": [],
        "source": [
            "AA_TO_INDEX = {aa: i + 1 for i, aa in enumerate(AMINO_ACIDS)}\n",
            "PAD_TOKEN = 0\n",
            "VOCAB_SIZE = len(AMINO_ACIDS) + 1\n",
            "\n",
            "def encode_sequence(sequence):\n",
            "    return [AA_TO_INDEX[aa] for aa in sequence]\n",
            "\n",
            "encoded_sequences = [encode_sequence(r['sequence']) for r in cleaned_records]\n",
            "MAX_LENGTH = max(len(seq) for seq in encoded_sequences)\n",
            "\n",
            "X = pad_sequences(\n",
            "    encoded_sequences,\n",
            "    maxlen=MAX_LENGTH,\n",
            "    padding='post',\n",
            "    truncating='post',\n",
            "    value=PAD_TOKEN,\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "print('Vocabulary size:', VOCAB_SIZE)\n",
            "print('Maximum sequence length:', MAX_LENGTH)\n",
            "print('Encoded matrix shape:', X.shape)"
        ]
    },
    {
        "cell_type": "markdown",
        "metadata": {},
        "source": [
            "# 🧠 Deep-Learning Sequence Encoder\n\n",
            "Architecture:\n\n",
            "```text\n",
            "Protein Sequence\n",
            "      ↓\n",
            "Amino-Acid Tokens\n",
            "      ↓\n",
            "Embedding\n",
            "      ↓\n",
            "1D Convolution\n",
            "      ↓\n",
            "Global Max Pooling\n",
            "      ↓\n",
            "Dense Representation\n",
            "      ↓\n",
            "Latent Representation\n",
            "```\n\n",
            "This encoder is used for exploratory representation learning."
        ]
    },
    {
        "cell_type": "code",
        "execution_count": None,
        "metadata": {},
        "outputs": [],
        "source": [
            "EMBEDDING_DIM = 32\n",
            "\n",
            "encoder = models.Sequential([\n",
            "    layers.Input(shape=(MAX_LENGTH,)),\n",
            "    layers.Embedding(\n",
            "        input_dim=VOCAB_SIZE,\n",
            "        output_dim=EMBEDDING_DIM,\n",
            "        mask_zero=True,\n",
            "        name='amino_acid_embedding',\n",
            "    ),\n",
            "    layers.Conv1D(\n",
            "        filters=64,\n",
            "        kernel_size=5,\n",
            "        activation='relu',\n",
            "        padding='same',\n",
            "        name='sequence_convolution',\n",
            "    ),\n",
            "    layers.GlobalMaxPooling1D(name='global_sequence_pooling'),\n",
            "    layers.Dense(64, activation='relu', name='representation_dense'),\n",
            "    layers.Dropout(0.20, name='representation_dropout'),\n",
            "    layers.Dense(32, activation='relu', name='latent_representation'),\n",
            "], name='TP53_Sequence_Encoder')\n",
            "\n",
            "encoder.summary()"
        ]
    },
    {
        "cell_type": "code",
        "execution_count": None,
        "metadata": {},
        "outputs": [],
        "source": [
            "latent_features = encoder(X, training=False).numpy()\n",
            "\n",
            "print('Latent representation shape:', latent_features.shape)"
        ]
    },
    {
        "cell_type": "markdown",
        "metadata": {},
        "source": [
            "# 📉 Latent-Space Exploration\n\n",
            "PCA is used to obtain a two-dimensional exploratory projection of the learned latent representation. The axes are mathematical projections, not biological labels."
        ]
    },
    {
        "cell_type": "code",
        "execution_count": None,
        "metadata": {},
        "outputs": [],
        "source": [
            "if len(cleaned_records) >= 2:\n",
            "    pca = PCA(n_components=2, random_state=SEED)\n",
            "    latent_2d = pca.fit_transform(latent_features)\n",
            "    print('Explained variance ratio:', pca.explained_variance_ratio_)\n",
            "else:\n",
            "    latent_2d = np.zeros((len(cleaned_records), 2))\n",
            "    print('At least two sequences are required for PCA.')\n",
            "\n",
            "latent_df = pd.DataFrame({\n",
            "    'id': [r['id'] for r in cleaned_records],\n",
            "    'PC1': latent_2d[:, 0],\n",
            "    'PC2': latent_2d[:, 1],\n",
            "})\n",
            "\n",
            "latent_df"
        ]
    },
    {
        "cell_type": "code",
        "execution_count": None,
        "metadata": {},
        "outputs": [],
        "source": [
            "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 7))\n",
            "plt.scatter(latent_df['PC1'], latent_df['PC2'], s=110)\n",
            "\n",
            "for _, row in latent_df.iterrows():\n",
            "    plt.annotate(\n",
            "        row['id'],\n",
            "        (row['PC1'], row['PC2']),\n",
            "        xytext=(6, 6),\n",
            "        textcoords='offset points',\n",
            "        fontsize=8,\n",
            "    )\n",
            "\n",
            "plt.xlabel('Principal Component 1')\n",
            "plt.ylabel('Principal Component 2')\n",
            "plt.title('Exploratory TP53 Deep-Learning Latent Representation')\n",
            "plt.tight_layout()\n",
            "\n",
            "plt.savefig(\n",
            "    FIGURES_DIR / 'tp53_deep_learning_latent_space.png',\n",
            "    dpi=300,\n",
            "    bbox_inches='tight',\n",
            ")\n",
            "plt.show()"
        ]
    },
    {
        "cell_type": "markdown",
        "metadata": {},
        "source": [
            "# 🎯 Predictive-Modelling Architecture\n\n",
            "The following model demonstrates how the sequence encoder can be connected to a binary classification head.\n\n",
            "It is intentionally presented as an architecture prototype. The current dataset does not contain a sufficiently large, independently labelled cohort for defensible supervised performance claims."
        ]
    },
    {
        "cell_type": "code",
        "execution_count": None,
        "metadata": {},
        "outputs": [],
        "source": [
            "predictive_input = layers.Input(\n",
            "    shape=(MAX_LENGTH,),\n",
            "    name='tp53_sequence_input',\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "x = layers.Embedding(\n",
            "    input_dim=VOCAB_SIZE,\n",
            "    output_dim=EMBEDDING_DIM,\n",
            "    mask_zero=True,\n",
            "    name='predictive_embedding',\n",
            ")(predictive_input)\n",
            "\n",
            "x = layers.Conv1D(\n",
            "    filters=64,\n",
            "    kernel_size=5,\n",
            "    activation='relu',\n",
            "    padding='same',\n",
            "    name='predictive_convolution',\n",
            ")(x)\n",
            "\n",
            "x = layers.GlobalMaxPooling1D(name='predictive_pooling')(x)\n",
            "x = layers.Dense(64, activation='relu', name='predictive_dense')(x)\n",
            "x = layers.Dropout(0.30, name='predictive_dropout')(x)\n",
            "\n",
            "predictive_output = layers.Dense(\n",
            "    1,\n",
            "    activation='sigmoid',\n",
            "    name='predictive_output',\n",
            ")(x)\n",
            "\n",
            "predictive_model = models.Model(\n",
            "    inputs=predictive_input,\n",
            "    outputs=predictive_output,\n",
            "    name='TP53_Exploratory_Predictive_Model',\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "predictive_model.compile(\n",
            "    optimizer='adam',\n",
            "    loss='binary_crossentropy',\n",
            "    metrics=['accuracy'],\n",
            ")\n\n",
            "predictive_model.summary()"
        ]
    },
    {
        "cell_type": "markdown",
        "metadata": {},
        "source": [
            "# 🧪 Why the Predictive Model Is Not Trained\n\n",
            "A supervised predictive model requires reliable biological target labels and enough independent observations to estimate generalization.\n\n",
            "Training a neural network on the present small sequence set would create a high risk of overfitting and would make performance estimates scientifically misleading.\n\n",
            "Therefore, this notebook documents the architecture without presenting fabricated accuracy, ROC-AUC, precision, recall, or clinical prediction results."
        ]
    },
    {
        "cell_type": "markdown",
        "metadata": {},
        "source": [
            "# 📊 Proposed Validation Framework\n\n",
            "A future validated study should:\n\n",
            "1. Assemble a sufficiently large and biologically curated dataset.\n",
            "2. Define a clear biological endpoint.\n",
            "3. Remove duplicates and control sequence similarity where appropriate.\n",
            "4. Partition training, validation, and independent test datasets.\n",
            "5. Prevent data leakage.\n",
            "6. Establish conventional machine-learning baselines.\n",
            "7. Train the deep-learning model only on the training set.\n",
            "8. Tune hyperparameters using validation data.\n",
            "9. Evaluate the final model on an untouched test set.\n",
            "10. Report appropriate metrics with uncertainty estimates.\n",
            "11. Assess calibration and interpretability.\n",
            "12. Perform independent biological validation."
        ]
    },
    {
        "cell_type": "markdown",
        "metadata": {},
        "source": [
            "# 📐 Recommended Evaluation Metrics\n\n",
            "Depending on the future biological endpoint, evaluation should consider ROC-AUC, PR-AUC, sensitivity, specificity, precision, recall, F1-score, balanced accuracy, calibration, and confidence intervals.\n\n",
            "Accuracy alone should not be treated as the principal metric when class imbalance is present."
        ]
